  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ソケイ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BD%E3%82%B1%E3%82%A4",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110056892,
      "text": "ソケイ は、モクセイ科ソケイ属（素馨属）の植物の一種。落葉性の灌木である。ソケイ属の名前のもとになっている。属名の素馨は、10世紀の中国の美女の名前に由来する。オオバナソケイ（大花素馨）とも呼ばれる。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Jasminum grandiflorum」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jasminum_grandiflorum",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1368954712,
      "text": "Jasminum grandiflorum, also known variously as the Spanish jasmine, Royal jasmine, Catalan jasmine, Sicilian jasmine, is a species of jasmine native to South Asia, the Arabian peninsula, East and Northeast Africa and the Yunnan and Sichuan regions of China. The species is widely cultivated and is reportedly naturalized in Guinea, the Maldive Islands, Mauritius, Réunion, Java, the Cook Islands, Chiapas, Central America, and the Caribbean. It is closely related to, and sometimes treated as merely a form of, Jasminum officinale."
    }
  },
